<div style="max-width: 44rem;">
  <h2 class="h3">The short version</h2>
  <p class="lead">Project Broadsheet is a love letter to independent publishing. It exists because indie journalists, essayists, and small magazines deserve better than a choice between "pay a SaaS forever" and "wire up ten plugins and hope they don't break."</p>

  <h2 class="h3" style="margin-top: var(--space-2xl);">Why we built it</h2>
  <p>Every major platform asks the same deal: pay us monthly, and we'll rent you a publication. Leave, and your audience stays behind. Raise prices? Your archive is on our servers; what are you going to do about it?</p>
  <p>Project Broadsheet refuses the deal. Content is Markdown in Git. Readers are on your list. Hosting is wherever you want it — Cloudflare Pages, Netlify, Vercel, your own server. Fork it once, own it forever.</p>

  <h2 class="h3" style="margin-top: var(--space-2xl);">What we believe</h2>
  <ul style="list-style: disc; padding-left: 1.5rem; margin-top: var(--space-sm);">
    <li><strong>Your content is yours.</strong> Plain text, version-controlled, portable. No "export" feature required.</li>
    <li><strong>Your readers are yours.</strong> Newsletter lists stay with you. No platform tax. No forced discovery.</li>
    <li><strong>Independence is a feature.</strong> The ability to leave, change direction, or shut down without begging a vendor is the point.</li>
    <li><strong>Readers deserve care.</strong> Twenty-seven reader tools ship by default because accessibility and comfort shouldn't be someone else's problem.</li>
    <li><strong>Free forever means free forever.</strong> MIT license. No upgrade path to a paid tier. No "pro" features held hostage.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class="h3" style="margin-top: var(--space-2xl);">Who makes it</h2>
  <p>Project Broadsheet is built and maintained by <strong>{{ meta.maintainer }}</strong>. The public-facing website you're reading is designed and developed by <a href="https://www.pikespeakwebdesigns.com">Pikes Peak Web Designs</a>.</p>
  <p>The project is funded via <a href="https://opencollective.com/broadsheet">Open Collective</a> and GitHub Sponsors. Contributions — code, docs, bug reports, and ideas — are welcome on <a href="{{ meta.github }}">GitHub</a>.</p>

  <h2 class="h3" style="margin-top: var(--space-2xl);">What's next</h2>
